# CODEOWNERS — auto-assign reviewers for each file path.
#
# Reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Order matters: later rules override earlier ones. The first
# matching rule wins. We list the most-specific paths first
# (so e.g. a per-file rule beats a per-directory rule) and
# end with a default fallback.
#
# Each line: <pattern>  <owner1>  <owner2>  ...
# Patterns use CODEOWNERS glob syntax (not full gitignore).
#
# Owner placeholders
# ------------------
# Replace @liumingrui with the actual GitHub handles of the
# project maintainers. The first listed owner is the
# "primary" reviewer (the one who gets the auto-assignment
# notification); additional owners are "secondary" (they
# get cc'd if they are subscribed to the repo).
#
# For a single-maintainer project, list only one handle.
# For a multi-maintainer project, list 2-3 handles so
# that vacation / out-of-office does not block reviews.

# --- Production code (highest review bar) ---
# Changes to forge.py / templates / configs affect all
# papers, so they require a maintainer's review.
/src/tmaudit/forge.py            @liumingrui
/src/tmaudit/cli.py              @liumingrui
/src/tmaudit/templates/          @liumingrui
/src/tmaudit/configs/            @liumingrui

# --- Tests ---
# Tests are reviewed by the same maintainer as the code
# they cover, with @liumingrui as a fallback.
/tests/                          @liumingrui

# --- Build / CI / tooling ---
# CI workflow and pre-commit hook are critical for
# the project's "tests must catch regression" property.
/.github/workflows/              @liumingrui
/.github/CODEOWNERS              @liumingrui
/hooks/                          @liumingrui
/_check_*.py                     @liumingrui
/_build_pyz.py                   @liumingrui
/_act_*.py                       @liumingrui
/.github/dependabot.yml          @liumingrui

# --- Documentation ---
# Documentation is lower-stakes; a single reviewer
# suffices.
/README.md                       @liumingrui
/CONTRIBUTING.md                 @liumingrui
/CHANGELOG.md                    @liumingrui
/engineering_notes_verify_template.md  @liumingrui
/act_summary.md                  @liumingrui

# --- Community-health files ---
# These are public-facing, so they need a maintainer
# to ensure the tone is right.
/SECURITY.md                     @liumingrui
/.github/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md      @liumingrui
/.github/SUPPORT.md              @liumingrui
/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md @liumingrui
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/         @liumingrui

# --- Build artefacts (auto-generated, no review) ---
# tmaudit.pyz is built from source; do not edit it directly.
/tmaudit.pyz                     @liumingrui

# --- Default fallback ---
# Any file not matched above defaults to a maintainer review.
# This ensures a human is always in the loop.
/*                               @liumingrui